# Assessment engine

Keep modules separate and explainable:

```text
Protocol → Trial → Adaptive testing → Analysis → Profile → Longitudinal data
```

Intelligence = choose informative trials and estimate a threshold with uncertainty. **Not** an LLM chatbot or medical advice. The adaptive and analysis engines are deterministic and never call an LLM; the only LLM use is the advisory OpenAI QC layer in `openai-quality-control.mdc`.

Allowed: Bayesian adaptive methods, staircases, threshold estimation, sequential logic, consistency/QC. ML only if it has a real purpose.

Store trial-level data, not just a final number: participant ID, assessment ID, modality, trial number, stimulus level, response, timestamp, protocol version.

**First prototype:** real (simplified) trial engines for **tactile, thermal, and chemesthetic**. The oral-sensory profile is computed from those results, **not stubbed**.

Do not invent stimulus magnitudes, reference ranges, or clinical cutoffs. Justify protocols from published methods. Do not claim clinical superiority.

If an implementation is only CRUD/forms/charts, it is the wrong product.
